// Roster wave 3 — ELECTRIC + LIGHT SKILL KITS. DATA, not code (ADR-0006/0057).
// Stable ids are APPEND-ONLY. This is the FIRST part file the skills registry
// has ever had: 000-core.ron holds 1..=11 and carries no band claim, so wave 3
// claims 40..=49 and deliberately leaves 12..=39 unclaimed for core growth.
// 000-core.ron is NOT retro-annotated — the collision check reads actual ids,
// not comments, so widening the diff into that file buys nothing (ADR-0204).
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL: the ADR-0143 STAB gate requires every species to
// learn at least one skill of its own affinity, and Electric and Light had ZERO
// skills. A species-only wave-3 slice would therefore be red on arrival — which
// is why skills, species and evolution edges land in ONE commit.
//
// Two skills per affinity (RW3-01): a cheap high-PP chip move and a stronger,
// less accurate finisher, mirroring the Fire (1/2) and Water (3/4) core pairs.
// No sets_weather and no applies_status — a new field value is a mechanics
// decision, and this wave is content only (spec non-goals).
//
// COMMENT HYGIENE (ADR-0143 D7): full-line comments only, and never a bare id
// field name in prose — write id=N. The content scanners strip whole comment
// lines and then regex whatever is left.
[
    // Electric kit. Spark is the 40-power/25-PP chip twin of Ember (id=1);
    // Thunder Fang is the 65/95 finisher twin of Fire Fang (id=2). Reusing the
    // proven Fire curve keeps wave 3 out of the balance conversation entirely.
    (id: 40, name: "Spark",         affinity: Electric, power: 40, accuracy: 100, pp: 25),
    (id: 41, name: "Thunder Fang",  affinity: Electric, power: 65, accuracy: 95,  pp: 15),
    // Light kit. Glimmer mirrors Spark. Radiant Lance trades accuracy and PP for
    // the wave's highest power: Light is mutually super-effective with Dark and
    // resists nothing either way (content/type_chart.ron), so the Light line
    // needs a real payoff move against the doubled Dark roster (ADR-0204).
    (id: 42, name: "Glimmer",       affinity: Light,    power: 40, accuracy: 100, pp: 25),
    (id: 43, name: "Radiant Lance", affinity: Light,    power: 70, accuracy: 90,  pp: 10),
]
